    "This is the only file to edit for the credits on /vfx/. After you save it, regenerate the page with: python3 vfx/build.py",
    "role, studio, year: fill in any of these strings. The line under the show title joins only the fields you filled, separated by ' · '. Leave all three as empty strings and that second line is left out. Do not type placeholder words such as Role, Studio, or Year.",
    "Selected work: set selected to true to feature a title, or false to keep it in All credits only. Selected work lists entries with selected true, in the order they appear here. All credits lists the others, in the order they appear here.",
    "image is the file name inside images/vfx/ (for example westworld.jpg). category is Film, TV, Games, or Commercial. Filters use the category; it is not printed under the title. The line under the title is only role, studio, and year. Commercial is Kraken Rum: it stays in All and is hidden by the Film, TV, and Games filters."
